parable('bare-rock','Soil on a bare rock','2:264','Giving','Al-Tafsir al-Muyassar links the rock washed bare to giving for display and to the loss of reward through reminders and injury.', [('Rock with soil','A smooth rock carries a covering of soil.'),('Heavy rain','The rain falls on it.'),('Washed bare','The rock is left bare. Read the warning about giving at the start of the verse.')], 'What does the rain leave behind?','A bare rock',['A double harvest','A river of milk','A growing forest'],'Compare the opening warning about reminders and injury with the physical image.')
parable('high-garden','A garden on high ground','2:265','Giving','Al-Tafsir al-Muyassar compares sincere giving with a fertile elevated garden that benefits from rain or drizzle.', [('High ground','A garden stands on elevated ground.'),('Heavy rain or drizzle','Both forms of rainfall appear in the verse.'),('Fruit','The garden gives its yield. The comparison concerns spending seeking Allah’s pleasure.')], 'What can suffice when heavy rain does not fall?','Drizzle',['A lightning strike','A stone wall','A fierce wind'],'Read this beside 2:264. What does each image emphasize about the act of giving?')
parable('rooted-tree','A good word and a rooted tree','14:24-27','Faith','Al-Tafsir al-Muyassar identifies the good word with the declaration of Allah’s oneness and describes faith through the image of rootedness and fruit.', [('Firm root','The good tree has a firm root.'),('Reaching branches','Its branches reach toward the sky.'),('Fruit','It bears fruit by its Lord’s permission. The passage also contrasts an uprooted tree.')], 'What distinguishes the good tree?','A firm root',['No branches','No fruit','An uprooted trunk'],'Follow both the good and bad tree images in the complete selected passage.')
parable('two-gardens','Two gardens and a conversation','18:32-44','Possessions','Al-Tafsir al-Muyassar describes a proud garden owner, his believing companion’s reminder, and the loss of the garden.', [('Abundance','Gardens, palms, crops, and a river open the account.'),('Conversation','The owner boasts. His companion reminds him of his Creator.'),('Loss','The fruit is destroyed, and the owner regrets his earlier association of partners.')], 'What does the companion remind the owner about?','His Creator',['A guaranteed permanent harvest','A journey to Midian','A missing ship'],'Read each speaker’s words before drawing a conclusion. This diagram summarizes a sequence, not an invented scene.')
parable('scattered-growth','Growth scattered by the wind','18:45','Worldly life','Al-Tafsir al-Muyassar connects rain-fed vegetation that becomes scattered dry matter with the beauty and passing nature of worldly life.', [('Rain','Water comes down from the sky.'),('Growth','The vegetation flourishes through it.'),('Dry fragments','The growth becomes dry matter scattered by winds.')], 'What scatters the dry growth?','The winds',['The ants','The ship','The lamps'],'Notice how quickly the image moves from flourishing vegetation to scattered fragments.')
parable('lamp','A niche, a lamp, and light','24:35','Guidance','Al-Tafsir al-Muyassar and Al-Jalalayn relate the lamp comparison to guidance in the believer’s heart. This diagram follows the named imagery; it does not depict Allah.', [('Niche','The verse names a niche containing a lamp.'),('Lamp in glass','The glass is compared with a shining star.'),('Light upon light','The verse speaks of oil, light, and Allah guiding whom He wills.')], 'Where is the lamp in the comparison?','In a niche, enclosed in glass',['Inside a ship','Under a bare rock','On an uprooted tree'],'Read both cited commentaries. The labels describe the comparison’s imagery, not the divine essence.')
parable('spider-house','The spider’s house','29:41','Reliance','Al-Tafsir al-Muyassar compares reliance on protectors besides Allah with a spider’s house that cannot provide the hoped-for protection.', [('Seeking protection','The comparison begins with taking protectors besides Allah.'),('A spider’s house','A spider builds a house.'),('Fragile refuge','The verse calls it the frailest of houses. This is a comparison about reliance, not a claim about material tensile strength.')], 'What is described as the frailest of houses?','The spider’s house',['A stone fortress','A ship','A niche'],'Keep the stated comparison in view rather than turning it into a modern materials-science claim.')
parable('shared-masters','Conflicting masters and one master','39:29','Faith','Al-Tafsir al-Muyassar contrasts a person claimed by quarrelling partners with one belonging to a single master, explaining a comparison of divided worship and faith.', [('Quarrelling partners','One person belongs to partners at odds.'),('One master','The other belongs entirely to one master.'),('A question','The verse asks whether the two are equal in comparison.')], 'How are the partners described?','At odds with one another',['Always in agreement','As gardeners','As sailors'],'Notice the contrast between conflicting demands and a single master, then read the commentary.')
