parable('mountain','A mountain humbled','59:21','Reflection','Al-Tafsir al-Muyassar describes this comparison as an invitation to reflect on the Quran and understand its meanings.', [('The Quran','The verse asks us to consider its revelation upon a mountain.'),('A mighty mountain','The mountain is described as humbled and split through fear of Allah.'),('Reflection','The verse says these comparisons are given so people may reflect.')], 'What response is named at the end of the verse?','Reflection',['Trade','Travel','Harvesting'],'Acknowledge the force of the comparison before adding a personal reflection. No mountain event is reconstructed here.')
parable('carried-books','Carrying books and bearing responsibility','62:5','Responsibility','Al-Tafsir al-Muyassar explains the comparison as carrying the Torah without acting on it, like a donkey bearing books without understanding them.', [('Entrusted with scripture','The verse identifies those entrusted with the Torah.'),('A load of books','The comparison names a donkey carrying books.'),('Responsibility','The commentary distinguishes carrying a text from benefiting through acting on it.')], 'What is carried in the comparison?','Books',['Grain','A lamp','A throne'],'Read the original context. What distinction does the commentary make between carrying a text and acting on it?')
